Error [jet.UseAfterMove]: `s` was consumed by `.loop()`, so it can't be used here
  --> tests/ui/loop_stream_reuse.jet:12:15
    |
 12 |     loop x in s -> print("{x}")
    |               ^
  --> tests/ui/loop_stream_reuse.jet:11:15
    |
 11 |     loop x in s -> print("{x}")
    |               ^ `s` moved to `.loop()` here
 Why: After a value moves somewhere else, its old name no longer gives access to it
 Fix: Stop using `s` after the move, or give `.loop()` a copy with `s.copy()` where it moved.
 Note: `s` is one-pass and cannot be copied — create a fresh source for the second drive
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0121
